			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2232467">
									

<p>I already expressed my thoughts on this, but for clarity:</p>
<p>I dislike this largely due to the gimmick that you're using to convey the story of these two Foundations communicating with each other. The references are aggravating to read, and it makes it hard to keep reading. The tone and character of the other Foundation seems very snarky (in a bad way) and is hard to want to care for. There's also the question of this playing out in a document, when&#8230; why not use a test page for that? It makes the whole thing seem unprofessional.</p>
<p>The anomaly itself, while interesting, doesn't feel like it plays out this well with all of the above. There's story potential here, but the article is frustrating to work with and read to get any sense of involvement in it at all.</p>

