			<div class="content" id="post-content-2233048">
									

<p>I enjoyed this one a lot. I didn't really grok the footnotes differences until pretty far into the article and had to go back for clarity's sake, but it wasn't a Herculean trial.</p>
<p>Edit: I'd also say this isn't a case of the format screw/bit of coding really making the article, but it was an interesting supporting element.</p>
<p>(Also, I wasn't sure if you were referencing David Rosen/IT stuff straight or distancing it in another universe, but it was amusing either way.)</p>
<p>The reason I like this, aside from it being well-written and on-point tonally, is that it falls into both the categories of &quot;Weird shit just happens around the Foundation.&quot; and &quot;The Foundation has to document <strong><em>everything</em></strong>.&quot; It's not quite to the level of absurd daily hijinks in, say, the S &amp; C Plastics canon, but it's still nice to see a bit of slice-of-life going around.</p>

