				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thedeadlymoose" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(732274); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=732274&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607633379" alt="thedeadlymoose" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=732274)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thedeadlymoose" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(732274); return false;" >thedeadlymoose</a></span> <span class="odate time_1424007650 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">15 Feb 2015 13:40</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2233129">
									

<p>I enjoy the <em>idea</em> of a gimmick, but you don't do much with it here besides <em>merely use it</em>.</p>
<p>This is one of our many articles recently that expects to survive merely by showing up and being well-written. It doesn't do much that's interesting; it's nothing I haven't seen before plenty of times. It has a <em>little</em> bit of fun, but not really very much.</p>
<p>But, indeed, it's in the positives right now, and may well survive, and the comment above cites &quot;well-written and on-point tonally&quot; as part of the reason for being upvoted. That is&#8230; not great for quality standards, since being well-written with good tone should be the <em>minimum</em> standard for existing on the site, but what can ya do.</p>
<p>A nitpick unrelated to quality: It's kind of weird to note the existence of the alternate universe being treated as such a big deal.</p>
<p>Another nitpick unrelated to quality: I don't like the use of Rosen, aka the character whose concept is a meta-joke that he's utter shit at his job (and indeed that seems to be how he's used here), but I think that's mainly personal. It wouldn't merit a downvote from me, because it's hard enough to get people to stop freaking out about using named characters or avatars in the first place.</p>

							</div>

								
					
